Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted]

scrapli (the Python binding) vendors libscrapli (github.com/scrapli/libscrapli,
a separate Zig project) as a precompiled shared library per platform.
libscrapli's build.zig hardcodes the six targets it is willing to cross-build
in one `zig build --all-targets` pass (ffi_targets); riscv64 is not among
them, so scrapli's own setup.py (which drives this build via
LIBSCRAPLI_ZIG_TRIPLE) has no riscv64 output to copy into the wheel even
after it is told to build it. Add riscv64-linux-gnu/musl so the existing
target loop produces a riscv64 libscrapli.so. This patch applies to a
separate clone of libscrapli fetched at build time by scrapli's setup.py
(LIBSCRAPLI_BUILD_PATH override), not to the scrapli checkout itself.

diff --git a/build.zig b/build.zig
index c127da1..c86272f 100644
--- a/build.zig
+++ b/build.zig
@@ -15,6 +15,8 @@ const ffi_targets: []const std.Target.Query = &.{
     .{ .cpu_arch = .x86_64, .os_tag = .macos },
     .{ .cpu_arch = .x86_64, .os_tag = .linux, .abi = .gnu },
     .{ .cpu_arch = .x86_64, .os_tag = .linux, .abi = .musl },
+    .{ .cpu_arch = .riscv64, .os_tag = .linux, .abi = .gnu },
+    .{ .cpu_arch = .riscv64, .os_tag = .linux, .abi = .musl },
 };

 const examples: []const []const u8 = &.{
